{"resourceIdentifier":"4025","resourceName":"Strengthening rural livelihoods of smallholder farmers in tribal districts of Odisha,India","description":"The fragile ecosystem of the upland tribal regions in Keojhar and Mayurbhanj districts of Odisha have been affected by deforestation and rampant shifting cultivation practices causing extensive soil erosion, reducing the capacity of land to rejuvenate and affecting natural vegetation and water resources.In order to address some of the issues of the communities it becomes pertinent to adopt interventions based on improved land use planning, soil-moisture conservation measures and improved farming based agroforestry practices. This will not only strengthen the agrarian livelihoods of the tribal households, but also increase their food and nutritional security.The proposed project in the two districts of Keonjhar and Mayurbhanj is aimed at improving the livelihoods of the tribal communities by restoring 4000 hectares of barren uplands through plantation of forest and fruit tree species mostly in private lands. Additional components include land development, soil-moisture conservation, crop diversification and intercropping and promoting organic farm and pest management practices. The project will be implemented in 4000 hectares covering 3 blocks of Keonjhar district (Harichandanpur, Jhumpura and Champua) and 2 blocks of Mayurbhanj district (Udala and Khunta). The project aims for economic upliftment of the small holder famers through improved land use planning, increase in production and productivity, social empowerment of women along with enhancement of the carbon sequestration potential through such interventions.","location":{"latitude":21.934722,"longitude":86.721388},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2023-09-11","endExclusive":"2023-10-12","endInclusive":"2023-10-11"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"4025"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","va